  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><sup><strong>Source:</strong> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/574642/diamond-spheres-erudition-esoterica\">Diamond Spheres: Erudition &amp; Esoterica</a></sup></p>\n<p><strong>Prerequisites</strong>: Sense Motive 5 ranks, Investigation sphere.</p>\n<p>Whenever a creature within your analyze range uses telepathy to communicate (or other abilities that send or receive magical messages, such as dream or sending), you immediately receive a Sense Motive check to notice the attempt with a DC equal to 20 + the creature’s Will save modifier—you automatically succeed this check if the creature is scrutinized.</p>\n<p>If you are aware of such an attempt, you learn one of the following observations about the communication: the source’s identity and location, the emotional state of the source or recipient, or a specific person, place, or thing mentioned in the message. The creature must then attempt a Will saving throw. On a success, they become immune to this talent’s effects for 1 minute. On a failure, you can listen to both sides of the communication for up to 1 minute, after which you may cease listening, or attempt to continue listening, granting them a new save. If you spend 1 use of skill leverage, the creature does not receive a saving throw against this effect.</p>\n<p>This is a divination effect.</p>\n<p><strong>Associated Feat</strong>: Telepathy Tap (<em>Ultimate Intrigue</em>).</p>\n<p><a href=\"http://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/investigation#toc55\">Source: Spheres of Power Wiki</a></p>",
